  work.creature.macaque_whole_body_sources remains the mainline.


# HANDOFF - lane/visual-verify-20260918 (agent: GLM 5.3)

Date: 2026-09-18. Branch: `lane/visual-verify-20260918`. Base: master tip
c43d3363 (appearance integration). All mechanics through PowerShell .ps1;
python = E:\PythonChimera\.venv-hy3d\Scripts\python.exe; E:\PythonChimera
untouched except running its pinned interpreter; port 8127 avoided
(verified present-and-untouched mid-run); SharedBody*.json untouched.

## What this lane was

DYAD visual verification of the LIVE coupled-arm scene: render the live
state and judge it against expected physics, closing the loop between "the
numbers say it works" and "a human can see it works". Rule 0 record
(statement/prediction/falsifiers F1-F4) admitted BEFORE the run; it lives in
tools/science_funnel/visual_scene.py and in every manifest under
tools/science_funnel/validation/visual_scene_20260918/.

## Deliverables

1. tools/science_funnel/visual_scene.py - the harness: drives the live scene
   over GET/POST /earth_state on OWNED port 8191 (refuses other ports),
   five scenarios (free_fall, target_reach, contact_press, friction_stick,
   friction_slide), deterministic pure-Python PNG renders (state + energy
   ledger) from the recorded numeric state, structured judgement templates,
   sha-chained manifests, --verify (F1), --record-visual (the GLM judge's
   visual pass). Unit falsifier tests in
   tools/science_funnel/tests/test_visual_scene.py (9 tests, green).
2. tools/science_funnel/validation/visual_scene_20260918/ - the record:
   per scenario state_render.png + energy_bars.png + numeric_state.json +
   judgement.json + manifest.json; wrong_state_probe/ (corrupted
   penetrating-hand state FAILS the template and renders visibly below the
   plane); run_manifest.json.
3. run_visual_verify.ps1 / build_engine.ps1 / qualify_visual_verify.ps1 /
   publish_visual_verify.ps1 - owned engine lifecycle (path-guarded stop,
   port-release check), one-shot build, QUALIFY gate, guarded push.

## Measured results (live run, 2026-09-18)

- 5/5 scenarios FINAL PASS = numeric template PASS AND GLM 5.3 visual pass
  PASS (visual verdicts recorded inside each judgement.json).
- F1 byte-identical re-render: PASS all scenarios. F2 python FK vs engine
  body.position_m: ~1e-17 m. F3 corrupted state: caught (template FAIL +
  visibly wrong render). F4 ledger closes < 1e-4 J (repo live-qual bar
  1e-5 x10 for these 45-90 s windows; measured residuals 2.4e-6..2.1e-5).
- Falsified expectations (recorded in run_manifest.json): total friction
  heat does NOT discriminate stick from slide (mu=1 landing books 4.79e-3 J
  > whole mu=0.05 slide 2.0e-3 J); the (60,60) command stalls at
  (36.6,33.0) deg under the authored torque caps; friction_slide never
  freezes - it ends in a BOUNDED stick-slip cycle (steady rule |v| < 5e-3,
  hand bound ~1e-4 m).

## QUALIFY state (honest)

- graphify consumer: HONEST, exit 0 (rerun at final tree).
- evidence objects: exactly 11 (unchanged).
- funnel suite: my 9 added tests green in discovery; the suite carries TWO
  MASTER-INHERITED failures, both proven NOT from this lane:
  (a) test_coupled_scene...test_default_scene_bit_identical FAILS on a
  PRISTINE clone of the lane base c43d3363 with the IDENTICAL mismatch
  (computed 23d27409... vs pinned a7b36b53...): a stale pin that landed
  master-side (appearance integration); re-pinning is deliberately NOT this
  lane's move. (b) test_batch_appearance...test_rebuild_is_byte_identical
  ERRORs on any FRESH clone: it needs the GITIGNORED fetched artifact
  tools/science_funnel/data/phylacine/PHYLACINE_1.2.1.zip
  (.gitignore:313) that only worktrees which ran the appearance fetch have.

## Traps hit (host-measured; do not re-pay)

1. run_earth.ps1 Start-Processes the engine, which INHERITS the launcher's
   stdout pipe handle: capturing the inner powershell's output
   ($out = & powershell ...) waits for pipe EOF that only the engine can
   release - the caller hangs forever with no children. Invoke it PLAIN.
2. Windows PowerShell 5.1 parses BOM-less UTF-8 .ps1 as ANSI: one em-dash
   or curly quote breaks the whole script. ASCII-only .ps1.
3. runtime.json is UTF-8 WITH BOM (Set-Content utf8): read with utf-8-sig.
4. FK law: the hand marker is T_hand @ [hand_point_m, 1], NOT frame origin
   + local (the naive sum is off by exactly |hand_point_m| = 3.63 cm and
   was caught by falsifier F2 on the first live run - the harness worked
   as designed).
5. The engine steps on a wall-clock thread; a settled state is an exact
   fixed point for the damped scenarios (poll deltas 0) but friction_slide
   legitimately never settles (stick-slip cycle) - per-scenario steady
   rules, not one global bar.

